Track 2: "Who Told You the Glass Was Cold?"
- Story & Context: Recorded during a humid 3 AM recording session in an Euljiro glass workshop, vocalist Yoon Ha-eun tracked her verses while leaning close to the cooling kiln, her throat parched from the dry radiant heat and bitter barley tea. Between takes, she confessed to Mateo that the track’s off-kilter tumbao bassline mirrored the erratic cadence of love letters her grandfather had sent from Bogota before disappearing from family lore. A stray glass rod shattered against the conga stand mid-recording, and rather than punch out, Ha-eun leaned into the searing synth lead with the spontaneous hook, "touch the crack before the heat forgets who we were."
